<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Path to Permanency recently hosted a virtual training, <strong>Safeguarding the Path to Permanency for Foreign-Born Youth in Care</strong>, bringing together foster parents, Guardians ad Litem, social workers, attorneys, and other child welfare professionals to better understand how immigration issues intersect with permanency planning.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">For children in foster care who were born outside the United States, unresolved immigration status can create significant barriers to achieving stable, permanent families. Identifying these issues early allows case teams to pursue appropriate legal pathways while keeping permanency planning on track.</p>
<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1791751730427_10610" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>The training explored:</strong></p><ul data-rte-list="default"><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">How to recognize immigration issues that may affect children and youth in foster care.</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Immigration relief options that may be available to foreign-born youth.</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Why immigration strategy should be considered alongside permanency planning from the beginning of a case.</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Practical steps professionals can take to better support children and families navigating both the child welfare and immigration systems.</p></li></ul>
<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1791751730427_9578" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">The session was presented by <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://fosterbloomlaw.com/attorney/kelly-dempsey"><strong><u>Kelly Dempsey, Esq.</u></strong></a>, of Foster + Bloom Family Formation Law Group, who shared practical guidance drawn from her experience representing children and families in these complex cases. Path to Permanency is grateful for her willingness to provide this important education to our community.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">As part of the training, participants received a <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/79Pw5eycO/c?w=C0TjGohnZkGEP-bEX_ukr7mMMhpCQgwHRVJP2mPbbqY.eyJ1IjoiaHR0cHM6Ly9kcml2ZS5nb29nbGUuY29tL2ZpbGUvZC8xNzZ4UTZ4QnhCRnNROVNDRVl0NjJwRmRYbDFSVHFUZEQvdmlldz91c3A9c2hhcmluZyIsInIiOiIzZDZlNTBiZS0yZjEwLTQxZjMtYWY2NC03ODVlM2ExODJmYzAiLCJtIjoibHAifQ"><u>screening checklist</u></a> and other resources to help identify potential immigration concerns early in a case. The <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/79Pw5eycO/c?w=9QwO4-8BCDvEeNENWKiWHPd5UzIYICMoFlGkbH8t8ck."><u>webinar recording</u></a> and presentation are now available in the Members section of the Path to Permanency website. Membership is free and provides access to this and other educational resources.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Providing high-quality training is one of the ways Path to Permanency works to strengthen collaboration across the child welfare system. By equipping professionals and caregivers with practical knowledge, we can help reduce avoidable delays and improve permanency outcomes for children.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">If you have case-specific questions, Kelly encourages you to contact her directly:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Foster + Bloom Family Formation Law Group<br>Office: 919.710.8199<br>Email: <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="mailto:Kelly@fosterbloomlaw.com">Kelly@fosterbloomlaw.com</a><br>Website: <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="http://www.fosterbloomlaw.com"><u>www.fosterbloomlaw.com</u></a></p>


  










  



  <hr />
  
    

    



  


  
  <h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Upcoming Training Opportunities</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Path to Permanency also offers training on <strong>Permanency Planning Reviews</strong>—a key process for improving communication, accountability, and timely permanency planning.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Upcoming virtual sessions:</p><ul data-rte-list="default"><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>July 27 at 7:00 PM</strong></p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>October 26 at 7:00 PM</strong></p></li></ul><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">These trainings are eligible for continuing education credit for Guardians ad Litem, foster parents, licensed social workers, and attorneys</p>


  










  



  <hr />
  
    

    



  


  
  <p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" id="yui_3_17_2_1_1791751897898_5125" class="sqsrte-small"><em>To learn more about upcoming trainings, access webinar recordings, or get involved, visit </em><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="http://www.pathtopermanency.org"><strong><u><em>www.pathtopermanency.org</em></u></strong></a><em>.</em></p>]]></content:encoded><media:content type="image/png" url="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/6a947e1fc462510da6513955/7730551a-f454-4569-aef4-3de377055706/safeguarding.png?format=1500w" medium="image" isDefault="true" width="1500" height="992"><media:title type="plain">Safeguarding the Path to Permanency for Foreign-Born Youth in Care</media:title></media:content></item><item><title>What Happened After the Press Conference</title><dc:creator>Benjamin Nguyen</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2026 20:39:28 +0000</pubDate><link>https://flute-flugelhorn-43ff.squarespace.com/news/4q90t2fensjufnhfljhninx2qqaojx</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6a947e1fc462510da6513955:6ab2dfe5f881742c21b6563d:6ab2e781e118502fefa89f4b</guid><description><![CDATA[The momentum continues to build. Our team is excited and energized by the 
movement and shift towards collaboration. Read below for updates, future 
events, and how to advocate for a time sensitive issue today.]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">The momentum continues to build. Our team is excited and energized by the movement and shift towards collaboration. Read below for updates, future events, and how to advocate for a time sensitive issue today.&nbsp;</p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">NPR Interview</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">The county responded to WFAE’s request for comment following our 4/21 Press Conference which called for accountability for Permanency Planning Reviews. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/baPuOvco5/c?w=U-rf0RYy2zkP-yYEQjgQn2t4SV9F5IbP4FludVUVVRU.eyJ1IjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZhZS5vcmcvaGVhbHRoLzIwMjYtMDUtMDYvYWZ0ZXItZm9zdGVyLXBhcmVudHMtcmFpc2UtY29uY2VybnMtbWVja2xlbmJ1cmctY291bnR5LXNheXMtaXQtd2lsbC1pbXByb3ZlLWNhc2UtcmV2aWV3cyIsInIiOiIxM2ZkMDYzYi0xZmM0LTQwN2ItOGZlMC1iZDIwYmQ0MDI4MjAiLCJtIjoibHAifQ"><u>Read the full article here.</u></a></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">We are encouraged that our advocacy has prompted a desire to improve these critical case reviews</p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">State/YFS &amp; Foster Parent Collaborative Meeting</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Our advocacy efforts led to NCDHHS initiating a meeting between YFS and Foster Parents last week. We appreciated the openness from leadership and staff and the continued movement toward greater transparency and collaboration with foster families.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Several important points were clearly affirmed:</p><ol data-rte-list="default"><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Permanency Planning Reviews should be held regularly and include caregivers.</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Social Workers, not YFS attorneys, should be determining case recommendations.</p></li><li><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Foster parents are entitled to receive most information about the children in their care, with very limited exceptions.</p></li></ol><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">These statements differ from many of the experiences foster and kinship families have shared with us. Hearing them stated clearly by state and county officials will give us leverage as we hold ongoing meetings with YFS leadership.</p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">CMS-DSS Educational Liaison Positions Reinstated</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Charlotte-Mecklenburg Schools has reinstated the 4 CMS-DSS Educational Liaison positions housed at YFS in last night’s approved budget. For more than 20 years, these liaisons have helped students in foster care stay enrolled, maintain school stability, access immediate enrollment, and navigate education-related challenges across CMS and DSS.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">This year, 425 Mecklenburg youth in care attended 119 CMS schools and were placed in 46 different NC counties. These youth need continued educational support, as the CMS graduation rate for youth in foster care is nearly 40% lower than the system average.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">This decision preserves critical support for some of CMS’s most vulnerable students.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Thank you to each of our community members who wrote to their CMS BOE member about the importance of these roles!</p>]]></content:encoded><media:content type="image/png" url="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/6a947e1fc462510da6513955/6c00c42d-c2b1-46db-a783-eea8c78a59a2/press-conference.png?format=1500w" medium="image" isDefault="true" width="454" height="341"><media:title type="plain">What Happened After the Press Conference</media:title></media:content></item><item><title>↗️ Momentum Is Building for Permanency in Mecklenburg</title><dc:creator>Benjamin Nguyen</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Apr 2026 20:38:15 +0000</pubDate><link>https://flute-flugelhorn-43ff.squarespace.com/news/-momentum-is-building-for-permanency-in-mecklenburg</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6a947e1fc462510da6513955:6ab2dfe5f881742c21b6563d:6ab2e73869b9c050ccc57d33</guid><description><![CDATA[63 of you showed up—filling the room beyond capacity. One usher quietly 
told us he wouldn’t turn anyone away because he had been a foster child 
himself.]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Tuesday night was a turning point.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>63 of you showed up</strong>—filling the room beyond capacity. One usher quietly told us he wouldn’t turn anyone away because <em>he had been a foster child himself</em>.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">That moment alone captured what this movement is about:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">&nbsp;<strong>People who understand stepping forward to make sure today’s children are seen.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">We were especially encouraged that three key leaders from Youth &amp; Family Services (YFS)&nbsp;attended and made encouraging remarks to the core team. That kind of engagement matters—and it signals momentum (Ms. Rountree, Ms. Ragsdale, &amp; Mr. Brailsford)</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Our program opened with a 9 year old’s voice that grounded everything:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><em>“I came here today to speak on behalf of kids in foster care in Mecklenburg County. When you make decisions that impact them, I hope you will think about me.”</em></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">County Commissioner and Board Chair, Mark Jarrell responded audibly, <em>“I will.”&nbsp;</em></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">And people weren’t just present—they were deeply engaged. As former foster youth Colby Blackmon Knight shared afterward:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><em>“I was struck by how much the room was paying attention—people weren’t just listening, they cared. That kind of support stays with you, and it makes me hopeful that real change isn’t far off.”</em></p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">What's Next</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">We’re seeing real progress.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">In response to our continued advocacy, YFS has appointed Permanency Planning Team Leads to <strong>track, monitor and facilitate PPRs</strong>—a critical step toward ensuring children are not left waiting in the system without direction or accountability.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">YFS has also initiated a new policy to clearly delineate between Child &amp; Family Team (CFT) meetings and PPRs. This will ensure that the correct participants are invited and that the permanency planning for the child is not lost amongst the other important topics in CFTs. (See below for the full policy).</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">To ensure this leads to real outcomes, <strong>we have formally requested quarterly meetings between Path to Permanency, YFS, and County Commissioners</strong>&nbsp;to review implementation and track results. This is how we turn policy into practice.</p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">&nbsp;The Momentum Is Growing!</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>• &nbsp;100 foster parents and GALs are already registered</strong>&nbsp;for our <em>third webinar on PPRs</em></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>• </strong>Community awareness is expanding across media and leadership circles</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>• </strong>And most importantly—children’s stories are being heard</p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Watch &amp; Share</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">If you missed the night—or want to revisit it—watch and share:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">🎥 <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/bdPt0UgHO/c?w=7rkwJ39RMYeEZ37cJtnqUTaEEQYNSoe9rPxWB-NDOnY.eyJ1IjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHJvcGJveC5jb20vc2NsL2ZpL2c4MjhlcW8wYXpnMjA3b3czeTd6cC9QcmVzcy1Db25mZXJlbmNlLm1wND9ybGtleT1mM3BteWd0aTVtcG9vcXF0M3NmcDlobmN5JnN0PXZvdWxlMHdpJmRsPTAiLCJyIjoiOTBiZDI3ZmUtMzZjNi00ZWMwLTg2ODYtMTFhMGQyYTVkZTIxIiwibSI6ImxwIn0"><u>Press Conference</u></a></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">🏛️ <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/bdPt0UgHO/c?w=xicg-xrueYXtDLyCT-cgJnHF1A1b2iQz3mJ-rKuV1hA.eyJ1IjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZHJvcGJveC5jb20vc2NsL2ZpL2Fjc2lzMHB2M2kyN2d4NzZzNzc0ci9Db21taXNpb25lcnMtTWVldGluZy5tcDQ_cmxrZXk9cG54MHQ1ZnRnODEzcXV5Z2VrNjUyMjZvbSZzdD02bGg5bnNsZiZkbD0wIiwiciI6IjkwYmQyN2ZlLTM2YzYtNGVjMC04Njg2LTExYTBkMmE1ZGUyMSIsIm0iOiJscCJ9"><u>County Commission Meeting</u></a></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">🎙️ <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="O1npr zU7jc" href="https://pathtopermanency.org/so/bdPt0UgHO/c?w=XJWoMhnknT4x4KumqwKOXCArWPDR15Zz0F72rjcdoFw.eyJ1IjoiaHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZhZS5vcmcvaGVhbHRoLzIwMjYtMDQtMjIvYWR2b2NhdGVzLXNheS1mb3N0ZXItY2FyZS1jaGVjay1pbnMtYXJlbnQtY29uc2lzdGVudC1pbi1tZWNrbGVuYnVyZy1jb3VudHkiLCJyIjoiOTBiZDI3ZmUtMzZjNi00ZWMwLTg2ODYtMTFhMGQyYTVkZTIxIiwibSI6ImxwIn0"><u>WFAE Interview</u></a></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">This didn’t happen by accident. It happened because you showed up, spoke out, and refused to let kids lingering in foster care staying invisible. </p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Commissioner Laura Meier texted: </p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><em>“You guys were so good last night! You came across as a group who wants to help progress. The signs were perfect–so clever and informative and effective in such a simple way. Your speeches were also informative and inspiring. I truly don’t think I could give you any advice on improving anything.”</em></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">We’re building something real—and Tuesday proved it. </p><h4 data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Mecklenburg CFT / PPR Process</h4><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Below is the new process that has been shared by YFS leadership regarding PPRs &amp; CFTs. </p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">PPR meeting will be tracked, monitored and facilitated by the Team Leads:</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>Scheduling the CFT/PPR Meeting</strong></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">The Permanency Planning (PP) Team Leads will contact parents to explain the purpose of both the PPR and CFT meetings.  They will inform parents that they may choose to hold the meetings either separately or as a combined meeting.  Based on the parent’s preference, the Team Lead will then coordinate with the assigned Social Worker to confirm the meeting format, schedule, and time.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>Joint CFT/PPR meetings</strong></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">The Team Lead will begin the meeting with a standardized introduction, using a script to clearly explain the purpose of both the PPR and CFT meetings.  They will confirm that all parties are aware of the joint meeting and inform participants that the Family Services Agreement (FSA)  and PPR forms will be reviewed and signed during the session.  The Team Lead will facilitate the meeting, with the assigned social worker present and the meeting will be documented as both a CFT and PPR. </p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><strong>CFT held separately following the PPR</strong></p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">The Team Lead will begin the meeting with a standardized introduction, using a script to clearly explain the purpose of the PPR.  They will inform participants that the PPR will be conducted first with all attendees present. Documentation will be provided at the conclusion of the meeting.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">After the PPR concludes, the assigned Social Worker and/or CFT facilitator will conduct the CFT with parents, their identified support and other required team members.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK"><em>Note: Path to Permanency has requested further clarification on the 3rd party representative not responsible for the case and have asked for the script that explains the purpose of the combined CFT/PPR or the standalone PPR.  We will update you when we receive a response.</em></p>]]></content:encoded><media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/6a947e1fc462510da6513955/58b4148e-5f7a-4336-b9d4-46951c9a44f2/2026-04-21+18.33.47.jpg?format=1500w" medium="image" isDefault="true" width="1500" height="1002"><media:title type="plain">↗️ Momentum Is Building for Permanency in Mecklenburg</media:title></media:content></item><item><title>A Night of Triumph at SEED20: Celebrating Path to Permanency!</title><dc:creator>Benjamin Nguyen</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 20:35:59 +0000</pubDate><link>https://flute-flugelhorn-43ff.squarespace.com/news/a-night-of-triumph-at-seed20-celebrating-path-to-permanency</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6a947e1fc462510da6513955:6ab2dfe5f881742c21b6563d:6ab2e6af136f8f1bcc188404</guid><description><![CDATA[Tuesday night, the greater Charlotte community came together for a truly 
inspiring evening at the annual Seed20 event. Ten innovative organizations 
took the stage to share their 3-minute pitches, but for us, there was one 
clear standout. Josclyn Reed, Executive Director of Path to Permanency, 
delivered a passionate speech.]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Tuesday night, the greater Charlotte community came together for a truly inspiring evening at the annual Seed20 event. Ten innovative organizations took the stage to share their 3-minute pitches, but for us, there was one clear standout. Josclyn Reed, Executive Director of Path to Permanency, delivered a passionate speech. She masterfully told her story, grounding her pitch in how lingering case timelines steal childhood.</p>


  



































  
    
  

    

    

    
