  <p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">Together, we can ensure that Permanency Planning Reviews become the consistent, powerful tool for progress they are intended to be.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="_13-wL _2jbIK">—Path to Permanency Core Team</p>]]></content:encoded><media:content type="image/png" url="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/6a947e1fc462510da6513955/767d66cc-366a-45b3-9340-fca09c32fed8/successful-peoples-assembly.png?format=1500w" medium="image" isDefault="true" width="454" height="341"><media:title type="plain">Successful People's Assembly Focused on Permanency Planning Reviews (PPRs)</media:title></media:content></item><item><title>Our state’s foster children deserve a quicker path to permanency</title><dc:creator>Benjamin Nguyen</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 17 Nov 2025 21:29:22 +0000</pubDate><link>https://flute-flugelhorn-43ff.squarespace.com/news/our-states-foster-children-deserve-a-quicker-path-to-permanency</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6a947e1fc462510da6513955:6ab2dfe5f881742c21b6563d:6ab2e5221b547337f5db27ad</guid><description><![CDATA[Check out this OpEd by our very own Lydia Alexander, published this week in 
